{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592857-w-ta-in-nwod-rules","id":592857,"title":"W:tA in nWoD rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T10:06:59-07:00","id":592857,"title":"W:tA in nWoD rules","content":"Overall I see not too many issues in the conversion document. One large question I do have however is regeneration- Garou regenerate automatically while Uratha need to spend essence. Which is it in converting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:09:31-07:00","id":592878,"title":"","content":"Whichever you like better.<br /> <br /> Which do you like better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:59:18-07:00","id":592973,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, Uratah DO regenerate, just not so fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:13:34-07:00","id":592980,"title":"","content":"specifically, according to 2nd edition, Uratha regenerate 1B per turn or 1L per 15 min unless they spend essence to speed it up. in Garu form they regenerate ALL bashing and lethal per turn. these rates increase as you increase their Primal Urge rank. and both Uratha and Garou regenerate 1A per day.<br /> <br /> its not quite as good as Garou (1B or 1L per turn unless in breed form), but still pretty awesome and in someways more useful. it should also be noted that Uratha take less aggravated damage than Garou in that only specific attacks actually do aggravated to them like silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:45:46-07:00","id":593473,"title":"","content":"Yes, thats something there. In nWoD the damage types are more conservative. It is a little more hard to cause lethal, and a LOT more to cause aggravated. So... better to keep Uratha rating when using nWoD system, and Garou when using cWoD. Otherwise, you can end with unkillable Garou in a world without that much aggravated, or Uratha made of paper in a world with a lot of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T16:24:35-07:00","id":594218,"title":"","content":"My solution for combat? You'll have to convert over the rules for hp to utilize forsaken's combat system properly, but it will speed it up ignoring soak. otherwise just use all as you would in apocalypse. Healing, aggro damage all that. Unless you're really looking to use the nwod world view there is really no reason to do a full conversion, just take from the system what you like and toss out what you dont. <br /> <br /> If you do want to just use forsakens rules i'd learn 2nd ed. rule set from the new core and do as the conversion guide suggests, though maybe make them full on tribes instead of lodges (though lodges no longer have requirements so its whatever). <br /> <br /> For the triat you can easily make them idigam. The BSD can slot right into essence corrupted uratha (similar discussion in the forsaken forums a while back).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T17:16:25-07:00","id":594274,"title":"","content":"Well, he did said regeneration was the only issue. For me, I think best to mainly use Forsaken rules as far as possible. I allways found nWoD rules better writen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T17:43:36-07:00","id":594284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592857-w-ta-in-nwod-rules?p=594218#post594218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution for combat? You'll have to convert over the rules for hp to utilize forsaken's combat system properly, but it will speed it up ignoring soak. otherwise just use all as you would in apocalypse. Healing, aggro damage all that. Unless you're really looking to use the nwod world view there is really no reason to do a full conversion, just take from the system what you like and toss out what you dont.<br /> <br /> If you do want to just use forsakens rules i'd learn 2nd ed. rule set from the new core and do as the conversion guide suggests, though maybe make them full on tribes instead of lodges (though lodges no longer have requirements so its whatever).<br /> <br /> For the triat you can easily make them idigam. The BSD can slot right into essence corrupted uratha (similar discussion in the forsaken forums a while back).</div> </div> </div> </div>Idigam are way, way smaller than the Triat. Maybe some Urge Wyrms can be Idigam, because they're only Incarnae, but the Wyrm is three steps into &quot;stats don't matter&quot; territory. Its psychological problems became beings on par with Celestines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:08:32-07:00","id":594822,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, but they don't have that in forsakens world. It was more a way to incorporate them at a power level nigh unstoppable for the forsaken. <br /> <br /> For apocalypse I dunno if Id even include idigam in a conversion. Id likely just use a big nexus crawler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T10:14:47-07:00","id":595758,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Translation Guides&quot; were really designed to be guidelines and idea-generators, more than any real substantial or official mechanic rulebooks. They were purposefully written with great ambiguity for STs to decide how they wanted to handle the conversions, both in fluff and crunch.<br /> <br /> If you're using Garou in NWoD, I'd say that it's the concepts of NWoD, not the mechanics, that you would transfer over anyways.<br /> <br /> 1) Is the idea that a Garou literally comes into the NWoD setting? If so, you could either have him keep his unique abilities (regeneration is different, etc.) as he is a different creature than the native werewolves and see how that plays out--it could have its mechanical advantages and disadvantages that only really reveal themselves once the game gets going. The other idea there is that once the Garou comes through the &quot;barrier&quot;, their essence is transformed to fit the local setting (kinda like how all Garou become one Tribe in Pangea.) In this way, the Garou's regeneration mechanics now become that of the local CWoD werewolves and you just move on.<br /> <br /> 2) Are you just porting Garou into the mechanics/setting of NWoD? If so, just do what you want. If you like the NWoD rules for regeneration better for your story, then go with them. If not, go with the NWoD and keep the native mechanics. Give both a try and see what flavor works best for your game setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters 